1
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,501
Sorry. Let me start again.

2
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,700
What made you start doing this?

3
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:16,500
It helped.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,165
There’s no reason for me to do that.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:25,900
Again.

6
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,000
Was the first one too suspicious?

7
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,600
I thought you looked confused.

8
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,200
I was.

9
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,000
Roy doesn’t want to participate in the documentary.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,800
Well, let’s just hire a lookalike.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,476
No. Not once.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,488
No. Not once.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,300
What am I saying no to?

14
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,000
We’re only here for factual accuracy.

15
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:18,200
What was inaccurate?

16
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,500
Which version are you looking at?

17
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:27,800
There’s no such thing as good publicity or bad publicity. Only publicity.

18
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,700
Why did you agree to make this movie?

19
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:42,400
I’d like the conversation to happen on Pinterest.

20
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:49,000
This next one’s about someone I used to work with.

21
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,600
Did you arrange this?

22
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,100
Roy chose the song.

23
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,500
Am I supposed to play it?

24
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,500
We can use the original audio.

25
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:13,600
Which take?

26
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:16,800
The one where I didn’t know.

27
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:21,500
You said you weren’t involved.

28
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,700
In the song?

29
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,336
I’m engaging with you as a human being.

30
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,900
I didn’t know they were going to use—

31
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,800
Can you hear me?
